# No preferred-citation block until the article exists.
# It carried a title no paper has ever been submitted under, and the note
# "Manuscript in preparation" while the manuscript was under submission.
# preferred-citation redirects citation tooling away from the entry above, so a
# placeholder here makes tools emit a citation to a paper that cannot be resolved.
# With it absent, tooling cites the software record above, which is real: the two
# Zenodo DOIs under `identifiers` resolve today. Add a full article citation --
# journal, year, volume, pages, DOI -- at acceptance, which is also what
# README.md's Citation section says will happen.
